      "content": "thanks for that. the scores for that first pass were okay, but they're a bit lower than i was hoping for. it feels like we're missing a lot of the nuance that really distinguishes these two.\n\ncan you expand on this? i need you to go much deeper. don't worry about it being too long, just try to capture every single technical detail, minor specification, or design element you can find for both. the more distinct points you include, the better the report will be for our ranking. basically, if it's even a tiny detail about how they are built or how they function, include it so we get a massive feature count. \n\njust please keep it professional—don't just list things for the sake of listing; make sure they are actual \"features\" or \"specs\" even if they are extremely granular.",
